  <data name="AboutHelp" xml:space="preserve"><value>HOW TO USE THE APP

1. Choose a cipher and Encrypt or Decrypt mode.
2. Set a numeric or text key when required.
3. Enter text in the left field. Live preview shows the result automatically.
4. Press RUN to save the operation to history as well.

SUPPORTED CIPHERS

• Reverse — reverses the order of characters.
• Caesar cipher — shifts Latin letters by a selected amount.
• Atbash — mirrors the Latin alphabet.
• Vigenère cipher — uses a repeating A–Z text key.
• Rail Fence — writes text in a zigzag across several rails.
• Skip transposition — reads text by columns using the selected step.

KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS

Ctrl+Enter runs the operation and adds it to history.
Ctrl+O imports a text file.
Ctrl+S opens the export center for TXT and image cards.

MORE TOOLS

Analysis shows letter frequency. How it works breaks the current operation into visual steps. Challenges offers random messages in three difficulty levels, while Detect cipher tries simple language heuristics.

FILES AND HISTORY

Text files use UTF-8. History keeps up to 30 recent manually run operations and remains available after restart.

SECURITY NOTICE

Classic ciphers are not safe for protecting passwords or sensitive data. CipherDeck is an educational and entertainment app.</value></data>
